CMHC Affordable Housing Funding for Waterloo region.

35:21.830 --> 35:25.450
You're on again Ryan, go ahead.

35:29.760 --> 35:33.464
Can I just interrupt for a second? I'm in favor and

35:33.472 --> 35:37.000
I am in attendance. I wasn't sent the queue and nobody asked

35:37.040 --> 35:39.752
me how I wanted to vote on that last one, so could you remove me

35:39.776 --> 35:41.300
from being absent, please?

35:45.840 --> 35:49.256
Okay. Yes, we will. Thank you. Thank you.

35:49.408 --> 35:53.144


35:53.152 --> 35:56.984


35:56.992 --> 36:00.040
Are you going to start this,

36:00.080 --> 36:01.020
Fiona?

36:05.520 --> 36:08.824
The 8.1.2 CMHC affordable

36:08.872 --> 36:13.020
housing funding for Langs Drive in Cambridge.

36:19.290 --> 36:22.866
Ryan, maybe you just want to introduce what we're doing here and then if there's

36:22.898 --> 36:26.946
some legal or financial questions, we can defer to Fiona

36:26.978 --> 36:30.418
and Wayne if necessary. Is that fair? Yeah,

36:30.434 --> 36:33.602
no problem. Happy to introduce this one. Yeah.

36:33.666 --> 36:37.430
So this, this is a report with a recommendation

36:38.730 --> 36:42.674
recommending that we proceed to enter into an agreement with the Canada Mortgage and Housing

36:42.722 --> 36:45.900
Corporation. This is, this is a new

36:45.940 --> 36:49.212
way of Doing business with our federal government through this stream and

36:49.236 --> 36:52.680
has been the result of a number of years of advocacy on our part.

36:52.980 --> 36:56.892
We've always been able to accept grants from the Canada Mortgage and

36:56.916 --> 37:00.332
Housing Corporation. That's how we have funded several of

37:00.356 --> 37:04.076
our Waterloo regional housing revitalization projects to date.

37:04.188 --> 37:07.644
What we have not been able to do though is secure some of

37:07.652 --> 37:11.964
the very favorable loan terms that the federal government

37:12.132 --> 37:15.228
also offers us. And the reason that we haven't been able to

37:15.284 --> 37:18.744
access those, those portions of what they have

37:18.832 --> 37:22.040
on offer is because we don't have the ability to take out

37:22.080 --> 37:25.112
a mortgage as a regional municipality.

37:25.256 --> 37:28.632
So we have been advocating for them to consider changes to their

37:28.656 --> 37:32.264
policy to secure against a debenture model, which is

37:32.432 --> 37:36.104
something that we are able to do. So after a

37:36.112 --> 37:39.512
lot of years of work, we're now able to

37:39.536 --> 37:43.410
access that. CMHC has provided

37:43.490 --> 37:46.578
the terms in the report that's in front of you

37:46.714 --> 37:50.034
this morning. Both grant and loan terms are

37:50.122 --> 37:53.618
very favorable and will save us considerable amounts

37:53.634 --> 37:57.042
of dollars than what we have been

37:57.066 --> 38:01.026
able to access on our own through lending

38:01.058 --> 38:04.818
markets. So this agreement

38:04.914 --> 38:09.010
would allow us to enter into this

38:09.050 --> 38:13.110
deal with the federal government for our revitalization

38:14.150 --> 38:17.998
at Langs. So it will now have the loan component attached

38:18.014 --> 38:21.630
to it which is different from our our first two projects at Kings Court

38:21.750 --> 38:25.358
and Wilson Avenue. Hope that helps understand what this is

38:25.414 --> 38:28.250
and what the report in front of you is speaking to.

38:29.750 --> 38:33.438
Thank you. I have three councillors.

38:33.534 --> 38:37.118
Councillor Foxton. thank you and through to

38:37.254 --> 38:40.270
Ryan, So we have this

38:40.310 --> 38:43.388
in Ayr where a community group got together

38:43.444 --> 38:47.580
and conceived a loan and did Kirkwood Apartments and you

38:47.620 --> 38:51.276
have some housing units in there and it worked very, very well and they paid

38:51.308 --> 38:54.652
off the mortgage and they run the apartments well. Now the thing I

38:54.676 --> 38:58.080
wanted to ask about this is if we are doing the rebuild,

38:59.060 --> 39:02.716
what happens to the residents that are there while the rebuild's

39:02.748 --> 39:03.640
taking place?

39:06.100 --> 39:08.890
Mr. Pettipierre? Yep. Thank you Councillor.

39:09.230 --> 39:12.742
So all of our rebuild projects go through a significant

39:12.846 --> 39:16.758
relocation process. It's challenging

39:16.934 --> 39:20.330
work for staff and the residents.

39:20.910 --> 39:25.270
Langs, every tenant that was there previously has been successfully

39:25.350 --> 39:28.758
relocated While this build happens.

39:28.934 --> 39:32.182
they also get first right to come back to

39:32.206 --> 39:36.292
the brand new building again under rent geared to income terms

39:36.486 --> 39:40.200
when it's finished. So the short answer is tenants are relocated.

39:40.280 --> 39:43.848
They're supported financially as part of that relocation

39:43.944 --> 39:47.192
process and hopefully we get to welcome them back to

39:47.296 --> 39:50.760
a brand new and improved building when construction is complete. Thank you and

39:50.800 --> 39:54.712
well done. And one final comment. There's a youth and teen center

39:54.776 --> 39:58.200
built within it. will that be established in the new build

39:58.240 --> 40:01.800
as well? through you, Chair,

40:01.840 --> 40:05.400
Yeah, we've done some really cool work thanks to some staff that are here

40:05.440 --> 40:08.756
today and working with youth populations at this building In particular,

40:08.828 --> 40:12.180
we established a youth committee to help us through the design

40:12.300 --> 40:16.356
process and learned a lot from them along the way. So yes,

40:16.388 --> 40:19.764
there'll be youth specific centres and hubs

40:19.812 --> 40:23.604
here at this site and I think it's a

40:23.612 --> 40:26.404
really nice feather in the cap of the folks that have been doing this planning

40:26.452 --> 40:29.620
work at this site to enable that. Well,

40:29.660 --> 40:32.292
I want to thank you for doing all of this, for taking care of those

40:32.316 --> 40:35.648
that have to relocate for some time, for making sure they're taken

40:35.704 --> 40:39.152
care of, for welcoming them back, to creating even a better center.

40:39.296 --> 40:41.500
So well done. Thank you so much.

40:43.240 --> 40:46.672
Chair Redman. Thank you, Chair Erb. I would

40:46.696 --> 40:50.496
be happy to move this, these recommendations and I, I would just underscore

40:50.528 --> 40:53.792
this is a long time coming. This has been a lot of heavy lifting by

40:53.816 --> 40:57.696
our staff and Langs have been an outstanding partner

40:57.728 --> 41:01.342
for a very long time So I'm sure this will be successful. And the only

41:01.366 --> 41:04.782
way that we've reached the threshold of a Better Futures number when we

41:04.806 --> 41:08.670
went from 50 units a year to what we see 3,700

41:08.790 --> 41:12.318
and counting now, is because we have partners like this.

41:12.374 --> 41:13.610
This is a great development.

41:16.150 --> 41:19.518
Councillor McCabe, you were seconded. You'll second it.

41:19.574 --> 41:22.686
Okay. Any other questions? Comments?

41:22.758 --> 41:25.662
None. Use your eScribe to indicate your support,

41:25.766 --> 41:26.410
please.

41:34.060 --> 41:35.520


41:38.700 --> 41:42.596
I vote

41:42.628 --> 41:43.240
yes.

41:46.700 --> 41:48.480
It's carried. Thank you.

41:50.380 --> 41:53.534
More good work. onto item

41:53.582 --> 41:56.690
8.2, equitable services and opportunities.

41:57.110 --> 41:59.770
An update on the consumption and treatment services.

42:00.630 --> 42:04.478
We have a number of community partners and staff

42:04.534 --> 42:08.574
from the region here. Dr. Wang, do you want to introduce the report

42:08.662 --> 42:12.450
please? And the people that are going to be presenting.

42:15.110 --> 42:16.530
Katie McDonald,

42:20.240 --> 42:23.500
Tara Taylor, Jen Scott,

42:27.360 --> 42:28.220
welcome.

42:31.680 --> 42:34.840
Yes, thank you, Chair Erb and Council.

42:34.960 --> 42:38.856
So today we have an update for council on the wind down of the consumption

42:38.888 --> 42:42.840
and treatment services site and the startup of our

42:42.880 --> 42:46.570
HART Hub. Katie McDonald, one of our managers in public health

42:46.610 --> 42:50.330
will review the CTS closure and provide a mitigation

42:50.410 --> 42:53.950
strategy update. The HART Hub Co leads.

42:54.450 --> 42:58.986
Tara Groves Taylor, the CEO of Community Health Care in Kitchener

42:59.018 --> 43:02.506
Waterloo and on behalf of House of Friendship,

43:02.618 --> 43:06.330
Jennifer Scott, Housing Services Director will

43:06.370 --> 43:10.026
share an update and their plans for opening the HART Hub

43:10.058 --> 43:13.566
in Waterloo region. And finally, Lindsay Sprague

43:13.598 --> 43:17.050
from Sanguen Health center is also in the audience today.

43:17.350 --> 43:20.010
With that, I'll turn it over to Katie. Thank you.

43:23.990 --> 43:28.030
All right. Good afternoon. As Dr. Wang mentioned, I'm Katie McDonald.

43:28.190 --> 43:31.822
for the presentation today, I will go over the context related to the

43:31.846 --> 43:35.850
CTS closure and the initial HART Hub engagement process.

43:36.310 --> 43:39.896
I will also review how we are working with community partners,

43:40.038 --> 43:43.508
including the Harm Reduction Work Group on a mitigation plan

43:43.564 --> 43:46.932
for the CTS closure. Finally, I'll pass it

43:46.956 --> 43:51.200
over to Tara and Jennifer to provide an update on HART Hub. Next slide please.

43:55.100 --> 43:58.520
And there's the overview I just covered. So next slide.

43:59.980 --> 44:03.588
In August, the provincial government announced its intention to close CTS

44:03.684 --> 44:07.208
sites within 200 meters of of schools or licensed child

44:07.264 --> 44:10.280
care centers. This included the Kitchener CTS

44:10.360 --> 44:13.832
site. At that time, the province also launched the

44:13.856 --> 44:17.432
HART Hub Demonstration Project. CTS sites were

44:17.456 --> 44:21.048
given the opportunity to submit a business transition plan to become

44:21.104 --> 44:24.328
a Hart Hub. Public Health, as the CTS

44:24.424 --> 44:28.008
administrator and Sanguine as a CTS operator held

44:28.064 --> 44:32.216
community engagement sessions to discuss what a HART Hub could look like in Waterloo

44:32.248 --> 44:35.336
Region and identify leads.

44:35.528 --> 44:39.608
The community engagement sessions included partners from across sectors,

44:39.704 --> 44:43.240
the cities and townships in Waterloo Region. given

44:43.280 --> 44:47.320
the requirements of the HART Hub model which include supportive housing,

44:47.480 --> 44:51.912
access to shelter and transitional beds, mental health and addictions treatment,

44:51.976 --> 44:55.832
primary care and case management as well as feedback from

44:55.856 --> 44:59.832
the community, Community Health Care in Kitchener Waterloo and House of Friendship

44:59.896 --> 45:03.660
were identified as the co-leads of the Waterloo Region HART Hub.

45:04.100 --> 45:07.356
Both organizations bring a wealth of experience and deep

45:07.388 --> 45:09.720
commitment to addressing our region's needs.

45:11.460 --> 45:15.660
Next slide please. Since its opening in 2019,

45:15.780 --> 45:19.228
the Kitchener CTS has provided an important service in our

45:19.284 --> 45:23.404
community and was part of a comprehensive drug strategy. We recognize

45:23.452 --> 45:27.760
and are very thankful for the dedicated work of Sanguen Health center.

45:28.500 --> 45:32.028
Recognizing the importance of harm reduction, Sanguen and Public Health

45:32.084 --> 45:35.848
also led conversations throughout the fall to identify potential potential impacts

45:35.864 --> 45:38.620
of the CTS closure and mitigation strategies.

45:39.120 --> 45:42.888
These conversations included many local agencies, partners from across

45:42.944 --> 45:46.360
sectors and people with lived experience. From these

45:46.400 --> 45:50.904
conversations, a Harm Reduction work group formed to further identify and prioritize

45:50.952 --> 45:54.184
mitigation activities and develop a harm reduction strategy

45:54.232 --> 45:58.184
Moving forward. mitigation activities are underway

45:58.232 --> 46:01.912
and being planned. This group will continue to meet regularly

46:01.976 --> 46:05.380
to monitor initiatives and impacts and strategize future needs.

46:06.530 --> 46:10.710
Some activities identified by the Harm Reduction work group and underway include

46:11.170 --> 46:14.522
increased needle recovery through the WINS program which is a peer

46:14.586 --> 46:18.954
based needle recovery program run by Sanguen, Ensuring naloxone

46:19.002 --> 46:23.514
is available to community through the Ontario Naloxone Program, Continued

46:23.562 --> 46:27.162
harm reduction support for shelters through the Emergency Shelter and

46:27.186 --> 46:31.668
Harm Reduction Integration Initiative, also known as ESHRII, engagement

46:31.684 --> 46:35.156
with police, paramedics, and hospitals, supporting

46:35.188 --> 46:37.940
training and education for interested groups.

46:38.100 --> 46:41.812
In addition, we are working with the Community Services Plan to

46:41.836 --> 46:45.076
End Chronic Homelessness Co-creators group to fund harm reduction

46:45.108 --> 46:49.092
projects through their collective investment process. Now I'll pass it

46:49.116 --> 46:51.960
over to Tara and Jennifer to talk about the HART Hub.

46:55.580 --> 46:59.012
Thanks, Katie. Through you, the chair, and thanks so much

46:59.036 --> 47:02.272
for having us today. I too would like

47:02.296 --> 47:06.528
to recognize the wonderful work that was done by both the Regent and Sanguen

47:06.624 --> 47:10.096
through the Safe Consumption site. And it's unfortunate

47:10.128 --> 47:13.840
that the HART Hub is coming online by virtue of that

47:13.880 --> 47:17.440
closure. But we're so fortunate to be working closely

47:17.520 --> 47:21.408
with the region and with Sanguen as

47:21.464 --> 47:24.980
we work towards implementation of the HART Hub.

47:26.280 --> 47:28.540
As Katie talked about,

47:29.800 --> 47:33.712
we worked very closely right from the initiation of

47:33.736 --> 47:37.744
the HART Hub proposal with the partners here in the Waterloo

47:37.792 --> 47:41.504
region. And we continue to meet regularly

47:41.552 --> 47:44.700
with them as well as consult with them

47:45.000 --> 47:48.800
as well as potential users of the HART Hub and current users of the

47:48.840 --> 47:52.896
CTS as we try and build out

47:52.968 --> 47:56.586
the service model. I think one question

47:56.658 --> 48:00.750
that comes up fairly regularly is, you know, where is it? Where is it located?

48:01.490 --> 48:04.890
It's not located in one place. It is not a

48:04.930 --> 48:08.538
brick and mortar location. However, the anchor site is at Community

48:08.594 --> 48:12.150
Health Care in Kitchener Waterloo at 44 Francis Street.

48:13.810 --> 48:18.250
We knew here in Waterloo that because of the richness

48:18.410 --> 48:21.812
of the partnerships in this community community and the amazing

48:21.876 --> 48:25.252
services provided by a multitude of partners in a

48:25.276 --> 48:29.188
collaborative way in this community, that leveraging those partnerships

48:29.284 --> 48:32.660
at those places and spaces was the right way for us

48:32.700 --> 48:36.480
to go as we bring the HART Hub online.

48:37.900 --> 48:41.636
So our model is built on leveraging, leveraging those.

48:41.708 --> 48:45.780
So it will be across a number of different locations where we know

48:45.820 --> 48:49.788
people already have trusting relationships with providers

48:49.964 --> 48:53.436
and therefore will ease access into HART

48:53.468 --> 48:54.920
Hub as it comes online.

48:57.860 --> 49:01.900
This sort of lines up exactly with the integrated and collaborative

49:02.060 --> 49:05.436
model that we hope to, that we hope to roll

49:05.468 --> 49:09.244
out for HART Hub because as we know,

49:09.412 --> 49:12.540
as we engaged with key stakeholders through surveys,

49:12.700 --> 49:16.396
some of the things that were most important to the community, to the service providers

49:16.428 --> 49:20.444
and to the folks that we provide services to, are concrete

49:20.492 --> 49:23.884
pathways into services for change oriented

49:23.932 --> 49:28.140
individuals, coordinated services and

49:28.180 --> 49:32.012
coordinated services that actually have someone coordinating

49:32.076 --> 49:35.532
from inception through the entire

49:35.596 --> 49:39.548
service pathway, which we know is not linear. In fact, I think we refer

49:39.564 --> 49:43.018
to it often as a bit of a, What does Michelle call it?

49:43.164 --> 49:46.462
She calls it a traffic circle, I think, so that you're coming in

49:46.486 --> 49:49.902
and out of it at various different points and we want

49:49.926 --> 49:52.810
to make sure that people are supported throughout those different points.

49:55.110 --> 49:58.590
We also want to make sure that it's a self guided,

49:58.750 --> 50:01.982
self directed service option for folks that

50:02.006 --> 50:05.982
they see themselves in it and they see their individual journeys in

50:06.006 --> 50:09.772
those HART Hub services, wherever they may be in their stage of

50:09.796 --> 50:13.276
change. By April 1,

50:13.428 --> 50:16.956
we will have online our intake person

50:17.028 --> 50:20.880
or people, our coordinators, our care coordinators,

50:21.220 --> 50:24.636
the manager of our HART Hub services or several managers

50:24.668 --> 50:28.732
across the partners will be in place and some of the key services that

50:28.756 --> 50:32.892
will be leaving our CTS location, like the Rapid Access to Addictions

50:32.956 --> 50:36.486
Medicine program, will move over to Francis street for April

50:36.558 --> 50:40.246
1. We do know it will be a phased in approach to HART

50:40.278 --> 50:43.846
Hub services. So that's what will be available at inception.

50:44.038 --> 50:48.278
We are working now to build capacity to share information across key

50:48.334 --> 50:53.302
service providers and stakeholders so that access will

50:53.326 --> 50:56.534
be easy for folks, particularly to mitigate the gap,

50:56.582 --> 50:59.654
As much as we can, from the CTS closure

50:59.702 --> 51:02.050
on March 31.

51:04.750 --> 51:08.230
we made sure as we developed these services that

51:08.350 --> 51:12.182
we had services that crossed over into Cambridge

51:12.246 --> 51:15.810
as well as into our rural areas within the region.

51:16.190 --> 51:20.214
It was important to us that those pathways and that those services provided

51:20.262 --> 51:23.730
access to everyone across the Waterloo region.

51:24.030 --> 51:26.130
And so they are built with that in mind.

51:27.850 --> 51:32.226
We also ensured that there was an outreach and mobile component

51:32.418 --> 51:35.714
of HART Hub as well as sort of access

51:35.802 --> 51:39.310
across regular hours, like outside of regular hours.

51:39.770 --> 51:42.994
There's an operational table in place now with the key funded

51:43.042 --> 51:46.370
partners in the HART Hub and we are

51:46.410 --> 51:49.538
in the process of putting out an expression

51:49.554 --> 51:53.090
of interest for the strategy and accountability table that will sit

51:53.390 --> 51:57.222
atop the HART Hub. There's also a lived experience and

51:57.246 --> 52:00.166
community advisory table that are in the planning phases.

52:00.358 --> 52:02.010
I'll pass it over to Jen.

52:07.710 --> 52:11.014
So here on the slide, if you can go back a slide. Thank you.

52:11.102 --> 52:14.662
Here on this slide shows a little bit more in practicality what

52:14.686 --> 52:18.486
we're going to be offering here. So really we know that for people

52:18.558 --> 52:22.232
who are experiencing homelessness or precariously housed,

52:22.376 --> 52:25.976
have mental health challenges or substance use concerns, it can be hard to navigate

52:26.008 --> 52:29.272
the health care system. So the hub is really designed to

52:29.296 --> 52:32.984
help provide, provide guidance, resources and support

52:33.152 --> 52:36.424
for people along their journey. So we will

52:36.432 --> 52:40.024
be providing increased access and expanded hours to the services

52:40.112 --> 52:44.024
listed here. So primary care, mental health and addiction support, including the

52:44.032 --> 52:47.874
Rapid Access Addiction Medicine Clinic. We'll be providing culturally

52:47.922 --> 52:49.950
safe care for folks in our community,

52:50.570 --> 52:54.354
land based supports for those who, our Iindigenous community

52:54.442 --> 52:57.554
members, mental health and addiction supportive housing,

52:57.602 --> 53:00.710
which I'm going to talk about just after I'm done this slide.

53:01.290 --> 53:05.346
Employment support. So for folks who are struggling to get back into work,

53:05.498 --> 53:08.830
we are supporting the employment needs,

53:09.130 --> 53:12.946
community based mental health support, and then the very lowest barrier

53:12.978 --> 53:17.258
would be immediate access to showers, food, laundry, and peer support.

53:17.394 --> 53:21.002
And that would be available with again as I said, expanded hours.

53:21.106 --> 53:24.810
So we know that our services are needed Monday to

53:24.850 --> 53:28.458
Sunday, all days of the week, not just in on the working days.

53:28.514 --> 53:32.026
So really we're excited to be able to expand hours for folks

53:32.218 --> 53:35.978
to access service. With respect

53:36.034 --> 53:39.834
to the mental health and addiction supportive housing, $1.3 million of

53:39.842 --> 53:43.636
the funding has been earmarked for mental health addiction supportive

53:43.668 --> 53:47.092
housing. The Waterloo Region HART Hub will provide impact in

53:47.116 --> 53:51.364
this area in two ways by creating a 12 bed transitional

53:51.412 --> 53:54.852
housing program and rent supplements available for folks

53:54.916 --> 53:58.788
to make permanent housing more accessible. The Waterloo

53:58.804 --> 54:02.964
Region HART Hub transitional housing program is designed to support individuals

54:03.092 --> 54:07.460
experiencing homelessness who are also navigating addiction recovery.

54:07.960 --> 54:11.184
Many people in this situation fall through service gaps,

54:11.312 --> 54:15.072
especially those transitioning out of detox or facing

54:15.136 --> 54:18.384
mid level challenges. It makes it hard to access

54:18.472 --> 54:22.128
housing programs. So without targeted support they

54:22.184 --> 54:26.020
risk relapse, declining wellness and long term homelessness.

54:26.520 --> 54:30.080
So this program aims to bridge that gap by providing

54:30.160 --> 54:33.420
short term housing, addiction recovery support,

54:33.780 --> 54:37.164
life skills training and connection to community

54:37.252 --> 54:40.636
resources. Participants will have personalized support

54:40.708 --> 54:44.140
plans to help stabilize, build independence, and work

54:44.180 --> 54:47.676
towards permanent housing. There will be significant housing support

54:47.748 --> 54:51.276
on site to be able to transition folks from this program into

54:51.348 --> 54:54.400
permanent into a permanent tenancy.

54:55.060 --> 54:59.160
This program will support all genders and will be abstinence based.

54:59.630 --> 55:03.490
We anticipate that people will be in the program for about 6 to 12 months.

55:04.030 --> 55:08.182
We believe that this personalized support plan and the significant health resources

55:08.246 --> 55:11.622
from the HART Hub will help people to successfully transition

55:11.686 --> 55:15.222
into permanent housing. We're still working through some

55:15.246 --> 55:18.454
neighborhood engagement so I'm not able to share the address of this program

55:18.542 --> 55:22.022
just yet, but within the coming weeks we will be sharing this more

55:22.046 --> 55:25.250
publicly and are excited to share this new program there.

55:30.270 --> 55:33.526
Thank you. Last slide. So in terms of next steps,

55:33.558 --> 55:36.950
the CTS is planned to close March 31, 2025

55:36.990 --> 55:40.806
and the HART Hub will be beginning services at that time. Harm reduction

55:40.838 --> 55:44.582
mitigation activities and strategies as mentioned are underway and

55:44.606 --> 55:48.278
we'll continue to closely monitor and evaluate this change along

55:48.334 --> 55:51.742
with community partners including the HART Hub, Emergency Services,

55:51.846 --> 55:54.890
hospitals and the Harm Reduction Work Group. Thank you.

55:59.590 --> 56:03.054
Thank you for your presentation. We have some questions from Councillor James.

56:03.182 --> 56:06.910
Hi, thank you. Good afternoon. Thank you for your presentation, through

56:06.950 --> 56:10.958
you chair, Very key

56:11.014 --> 56:14.174
topic that I've had to navigate

56:14.302 --> 56:17.844
for a few weeks. So I do have a couple of questions just for

56:17.862 --> 56:21.016
clarification and thanks for all your work on this in the short

56:21.168 --> 56:24.664
timeline. But will the HART hub services

56:24.752 --> 56:28.872
be available to people who are not yet change ready in

56:28.896 --> 56:32.872
their addiction journey? What does that look like in terms of the work?

56:33.056 --> 56:36.900
And I have a follow up after. It's a great question,

56:37.520 --> 56:40.888
one that we chat about fairly regularly because change

56:40.944 --> 56:44.450
orientation, as I sort of indicated earlier, is not linear.

56:44.870 --> 56:48.654
So that's how we're defining accessibility to HART

56:48.742 --> 56:51.490
hub services is a change orientation.

56:51.910 --> 56:56.014
However, it doesn't mean that the services that are currently available

56:56.102 --> 56:59.646
for supports don't go away, despite the fact

56:59.798 --> 57:03.038
those teams are evolving and having additional sort of

57:03.174 --> 57:06.750
services added to them like addictions counselling and mental health counselling.

57:06.830 --> 57:11.016
So people will still be accessing the folks they trust, the folks

57:11.048 --> 57:14.744
they've built relationships with in the places they have those relationships,

57:14.792 --> 57:18.296
if they do. If not, they'll come through a different referral pathway.

57:18.488 --> 57:21.752
But depending on sort of where they're at in their journey is how it will

57:21.776 --> 57:25.352
be determined what those next steps to services are. Does that

57:25.376 --> 57:28.968
answer the question? It does. Kind of leads to kind of my follow up.

57:29.024 --> 57:32.792
So I'm aware that the funding was cut by 1.5 million. So how are

57:32.816 --> 57:36.930
we covering the cost of the essential services as

57:36.970 --> 57:40.802
a result of this funding gap? The funding cut to

57:40.826 --> 57:44.434
CTS you mean? Yes. Do you

57:44.442 --> 57:46.990
want to answer that question or do you feel good?

57:48.490 --> 57:51.510
Yeah, through the chair, I'll pass it over to Dr. Wang.

57:52.810 --> 57:55.910
Sorry, just to confirm.

57:56.890 --> 58:00.482
So the province will no longer pay

58:00.666 --> 58:04.590
for a CTS, but they will

58:04.970 --> 58:08.146
redirect that money to the HART hub. and that's

58:08.178 --> 58:11.538
the full amount that was initially directed to the CTS

58:11.634 --> 58:14.370
That's being directed to the HART hub? Yes. In fact,

58:14.490 --> 58:18.130
the province is committing more

58:18.170 --> 58:20.710
than the amount of the CTS.

58:21.210 --> 58:25.266
Approximately, They've announced approximately three times,

58:25.418 --> 58:29.334
but we don't have the specifics yet. So we're waiting still that

58:29.482 --> 58:33.422
confirmation. But yes, they're allocating,

58:33.486 --> 58:37.198
They're essentially reallocating the full amount

58:37.294 --> 58:40.286
that they would have paid for the CTS to the HART hub. Okay.

58:40.398 --> 58:43.582
And then, Sorry, chair, just as a result of that, I just have

58:43.606 --> 58:47.166
another question. It regards the employment piece. So the

58:47.238 --> 58:50.782
people who, you know, it may be

58:50.806 --> 58:54.238
a challenge to be employed and the CTS was employing them,

58:54.294 --> 58:57.880
are there any things to mitigate that? I'm conscious of that

58:57.920 --> 59:01.352
because we're in a financial crisis with everything right now. What is being

59:01.376 --> 59:04.504
